I left out the enrichment fetch. This node's `with` clause grants only `StateHandle<'subscriptions', read>`, which is `aap:caps/state-read`. Fetching a URL would need `aap:caps/http-client`, so the component would have more authority than the graph declares. The fetch also couldn't change the output, so it would only add a way to send data out of the node. To add it, the platform team needs to extend the graph's `with` clause to include an `HTTPClient<['metadata.internal.example']>` handle. The node can then be regenerated with that grant.

